# arena - the cycle region, and the way out of it.
#
# NAMES FIRST, because they overlap. A REGION is the runtime's bump-buffer
# mechanism; there are three of them (arena, frame, pools) and they all
# size themselves the same way. The ARENA is the innermost one, the one a
# cycle resets. This orb is the arena and the escape hatch beside it, not
# regions in general - frame and pools are not exposed here.
#
# Orion has no garbage collector. The default mode is plain malloc that
# never gives anything back, and that is right for a tool that runs and
# exits: nobody is left to care. A LOOP that grinds through a lot of data
# is the other case. It has to say where a cycle ENDS, and then the
# runtime hands back everything that cycle allocated.
#
#   arena_on()
#   loop:
#       ...everything the cycle allocates lands in the arena...
#       mine = persisted(must_live)      # out of the arena, into malloc
#       arena_reset()                    # the rest is garbage by definition
#
# `persisted` is the point of this orb. Without it there is no way across the
# line: a value born in the arena POINTS into it, and after a reset the
# next cycle writes over it with nothing to say so. Measured on a reader
# that grinds 256 MB in blocks: 1615 MB peak without the reset, 13 MB with.
#
# The externs live in runtime/orion_rt.c. app, typeface and orion_ir each
# declare their own copy of them today; this orb is where they belong.

external define orion_arena_on() -> int
external define orion_arena_off() -> int
external define orion_arena_reset() -> int
external define orion_arena_active() -> int
external define orion_arena_used() -> int
external define orion_persist_on() -> int
external define orion_persist_off() -> int

# --- the cycle ---
# no example: allocation mode is process-wide state - proven by tools/region_shrink_test.sh
public define arena_on() -> number = orion_arena_on()
# no example: allocation mode is process-wide state - proven by tools/region_shrink_test.sh
public define arena_off() -> number = orion_arena_off()
# Hand the cycle's allocations back. Everything born in the arena since the
# last reset is gone; reading one afterwards is a wild pointer.
# no example: allocation mode is process-wide state - proven by tools/region_shrink_test.sh
public define arena_reset() -> number = orion_arena_reset()
# Bytes bumped since the last reset. Useful to prove a copy really copied.
# no example: allocation mode is process-wide state - proven by tools/region_shrink_test.sh
public define arena_used() -> number = orion_arena_used()

# --- crossing the line ---
# Everything allocated between persist_on and persist_off goes to malloc and
# survives a reset. The arena is PAUSED for that stretch, not swept: values
# born in it before the pause stay readable, which is what lets you copy one
# out. orion_alloc gives the arena priority, so a bare persist_on while the
# arena is on does nothing - the pause is the whole trick.
#
# Stateless on purpose: persist_on says whether it paused, persist_off takes
# that back. An orb cannot hold a flag between calls, and a hidden one would
# be wrong the moment two of these nested.
#
#   was = persist_on()
#   ...allocate what must outlive the cycle...
#   persist_off(was)
# no example: allocation mode is process-wide state - proven by tools/region_shrink_test.sh
public define persist_on() -> number:
    was = orion_arena_active()
    if was is 1:
        orion_arena_off()
    orion_persist_on()
    was

# no example: allocation mode is process-wide state - proven by tools/region_shrink_test.sh
public define persist_off(was: number) -> number:
    orion_persist_off()
    if was is 1:
        orion_arena_on()
    was

# A copy of `t` that is still there after the arena is swept.
#
# `orion_persist_text` is the runtime's own evacuation: one malloc and one
# memcpy of the whole text, header included, straight out of whatever
# region it was in. NULL in gives "" out. log, orion_ast_to_ir and
# orion_driver already use it to carry a text into a slot store.
#
# It is NOT the persist MODE and needs none of the pausing above: it does
# not ask where allocation is currently pointed, it allocates from malloc
# by name. Which is why it is one copy and not the three a bytes_of round
# trip would cost.
public external define orion_persist_text(s: text) -> text

# no example: allocation mode is process-wide state - proven by tools/region_shrink_test.sh
public define persisted(t: text) -> text = orion_persist_text(t)
